    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1220">

                <pb facs="1342" n="1330" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg1330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">012.3/11–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé to the Polish Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-01T13:00:00-04:00">November 1, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Poles 24. Please deliver the following message for Prime Minister Mikolajczyk
                    from the President: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Personal for Prime Minister Mikolajczyk from the President. Your message
                            of October 26 is receiving my personal consideration. I very much hope
                            that your problems will be composed satisfactorily. I expect to send you
                            another message soon.”<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1220-f1"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1220-f1" n="9" xml:id="d1220-f1-content">
                <p>In a memorandum of November 9, Acting Secretary of State Stettinius recalled to
                    the President that “the Polish Government is waiting some further word from
                    you.” A short, suggested message was enclosed for the President to approve, but
                    it was not sent. After another reminder on November 15 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1334">p. 1334</ref>) the President approved the
                    communication which was sent to Mikolajczyk on November 17 (<ref
                        target="#pg1334">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>
                    </ref>).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
